<https://www.insperity.com/graph/change-log> {

  <https://www.insperity.com/resource/change-log/ChangeRecord/2026-10-22T020242Z-operational-areas> a prov:Activity , dct:ProvenanceStatement ;
    rdfs:label "Operational areas, naming standard and enterprise service catalog, 2026-10-22T02:02:42Z"@en ;
    dct:description "Operational areas and the naming standard (design decisions D25, D26, D27), at the direction of Jeffrey Wallk. Four operational areas: Commercial Operations (Sales, Marketing, Pricing, Customer Care), Business Operations, HR Service Operations and Technical Operations, each with shared Vocabulary, Taxonomy, Ontology and Shapes at …/<kind>/<area>/ and a taxonomy of its domains. Commercial Operations 0.4.0 moves from …/domain-commercial-operations/ to …/commercial-operations/. Customer success becomes Domain Customer Care 0.2.0; Pricing and contracts becomes Domain Pricing 0.3.0; Partner and channel becomes Domain Sales.Partner & Channel 0.2.0, an L2 of Domain Sales; Domain Legal 0.2.0 moves to Business Operations and takes the client service agreement, commercial agreement, clause, contract management steps, agreement terms and statuses. Every asset is titled by the naming standard (Domain Sales Ontology, Commercial Operations Taxonomy); dot-joined IRIs for nested domains. Primitives may be cited from any domain; classes, relations, concepts and imports stay within the core, the area, parent domains and the domain itself (D27). New: the APQC PCF 7.2.1 reference registry (category 3.0, 199 elements, one owner per element) and the enterprise service catalog 0.1.0 (internal and external portfolios). The Sales assembly 0.4.0 and Sales value map 0.2.0 are re-released against Commercial Operations 0.4.0. Built by build_domains.py, build_reference.py, build_assembly.py and build_catalog.py against Baseline Core v1.0 (core 0.1.0), which was read and not changed; 0 errors."@en ;
    dct:creator "Jeffrey Wallk" ;
    dct:contributor "Claude (AI assistant), at the direction of Jeffrey Wallk" ;
    prov:startedAtTime "2026-10-22T02:02:42Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
